modules.details_md:
The docstring lists the package's main parts in the order a look flows through them:

- the map itself, from the game's own data (`mapdata`);
- her position from her minimap dot, refined by what's on screen (`pose`);
- monsters placed on their platforms and tracked from look to look (`monsters`);
- one look placed on the map, with the drops on the ground (`scene`);
- every look taken through `Senses` (`senses`).

The package has grown since: the scene locator (`locate`, `camreg`, `mapart`, `her_cues`), the continuous feed (`feed`, `service`, `worldstate`, `tracking`), her memory of monsters and other modules live here too. The layer rule is the important part: `tests/test_architecture.py` maps `"localization": {"perception"}`, so localization code can use perception and the shared modules (paths, screen geometry, telemetry, native code, the character profile) but never motion, attack, control or behavior.
